<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">CORFO</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Production Development Corporation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">CORFO, the Production Development Corporation, is a Chilean state agency founded in 1939 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popular-front-chile">Popular Front</a> government of Pedro Aguirre Cerda, after the Chillán earthquake. It financed and created key national enterprises in electricity, oil, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, becoming the main instrument of state-led industrialisation. It continues to support innovation and private enterprise.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corfo.jpg" alt="CORFO" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorge Barrios · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peso_Chileno_1933.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
